{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["And she called her name Dinah — no expression of praise was written for the birth of a daughter, to explain why she was so named, for they do not give praise for a daughter as for a son. And its purpose is to inform you that all the sons of Jacob were males except for this one. So too: ושם בת אשר סרח. Among all seventy souls there were only two females: Yocheved and Serach."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:46.120996801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}